### recall.select - Memory store & recall
# Self-contained: creates a user + project, stores memories, then recalls them.
# Storing embeds the text and upserts it into the (user, project) Qdrant collection.
# (JetBrains HTTP client format.)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### Setup: create a user
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "email": "memory@example.com"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("userId", response.body.id);
%}

### Setup: create a project
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/projects
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "name": "default"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("projectId", response.body.id);
%}

### Store a memory -> 201 (collection auto-provisioned on first write)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/projects/{{projectId}}/memories
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "text": "The user prefers dark mode and terse answers.",
    "metadata": { "tag": "preference" }
}

### Store another memory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/projects/{{projectId}}/memories
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "text": "The project ships as Docker containers behind a shared Caddy proxy."
}

### Recall - nearest memories to a query (closest first)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}/projects/{{projectId}}/memories/search
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "query": "how does the user like their answers?",
    "limit": 5
}
